{# A FULL-WIDTH BAND above a two-column layout, answering three questions in one
   glance: where does this stand (`flow`), what was done (`summary`), and what
   evidence is there (`links`).

   THREE SLOTS, NOT FOUR. It carried an `actions` region declared for a
   transition control that had been removed at a review gate and never refilled.
   Measured across every scene composing this band, all three fill `flow`,
   `summary` and `links` and none fills `actions` — so the region was not a
   shape held open for later, it was one more thing every reader of this file had
   to account for. Adding it back is a line of YAML and a `{% if %}` at the
   moment somebody has a band action to place.

   THE LINKS SIT BELOW THE SUMMARY, NOT BESIDE IT (C21). The first iteration put
   them in a second column of the body row, and the human read that as two
   things competing for one glance. Stacked, the band reads top to bottom in the
   order the questions are asked, and the link groups get the full width — so
   they lay out as one wrapping row of groups instead of a narrow gutter that
   wraps every label. Slot order is unchanged: flow, summary, links, in the DOM
   and on screen.

   IT IS COMPACT: about 150 px for a one-line summary at compact density. The
   padding and the gaps between regions are small because the summary's own
   entry brings its vertical padding, and on a wide screen the summary region
   lays its parts out side by side, so an entry's link and action sit beside
   it rather than under it. The flow's parts, a status badge and the chain,
   share one wrapping row too.

   IT KNOWS NOTHING ABOUT WHAT IT SUMMARISES. The three questions are asked of a
   release, a run and a deployment in the same words; every region renders only
   when its slot is filled, so a caller with two of the three gets a band of
   two. #}
<div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass(['summary-band', 'flex', 'flex-col', 'gap-inline-xs', 'py-inline', 'px-group', 'xl:px-gutter', 'bg-surface-2', 'border', 'border-border', 'rounded-sm']) }}>
  {% if flow %}
    <div class="summary-band__header flex items-center justify-between gap-stack flex-wrap">
      <div class="summary-band__flow min-w-0 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-inline">{% block flow %}{{ flow }}{% endblock %}</div>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if summary or links %}
    <div class="summary-band__body flex flex-col gap-inline-xs">
      {% if summary %}<div class="summary-band__summary min-w-0 flex flex-col gap-inline-xs lg:flex-row lg:items-center lg:gap-group">{% block summary %}{{ summary }}{% endblock %}</div>{% endif %}
      {% if links %}<div class="summary-band__links min-w-0 flex flex-wrap items-start gap-x-[28px] gap-y-stack">{% block links %}{{ links }}{% endblock %}</div>{% endif %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
